WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.610
Table football was first patented by a
British inventor in 1923.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.410
It became popular throughout Europe with
leagues forming by the 1950s.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.300
A decade later, an American working in West
Germany brought the game to the US,

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.490
trademarking the German word for it
foosball.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.280
In France, the game of foosball is known as
Babyfoot.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.460
This company produces ready made as well as
custom made tables like this one featuring

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.630
biker players.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:35.400
Production begins at a foundry where workers
melt down bars of aluminum.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:42.380
An injection molding machine shoots the
molten aluminum into molds in the shape of

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:48.380
players. A robot removes the casting from
the injection machine.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:53.870
The mold yields four players, each one
sporting the manufacturer's name on the front

00:00:53.870 --> 00:01:01.370
of his jersey. A worker places each casting
on a press, then with one strike separates

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.920
the four players and cuts off excess metal.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.610
A computer guided machine drills a hole in
the center of each player through which the

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.780
rod will pass.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:21.430
Then the machine threads a hole through the
players back for the screw that secures the

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:22.630
player to the rod.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:29.840
Another machine saws a two millimeter gap in
the back to allow clearance for a screwdriver

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.670
to tighten the player onto the rod.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:40.130
Once ready, the players move to the foosball
table factory where a worker sprays on a base

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:41.270
coat of white paint.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:50.290
Once that dries, workers continue painting
the players, but now using an airbrush, they

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:52.510
mask the players body to paint only his
head.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:56.680
The company offers a selection of skin tones.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:02.230
Then they mask the player with another
stencil covering the skin and exposing the

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.520
shirt and socks.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.300
Next. They mask everything except the
player's head and feet.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.930
A player can be brunette, blonde or redhead.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:15.730
They paint the shoes black.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.680
Then the player's eyes and mouth.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:22.780
Manufacturers construct the table out of
solid beech.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:27.610
A computer guided milling machine profiles
the wood components, drills the required

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:30.370
holes, and engraves the company name.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:38.810
Workers then assemble the parts, starting
with the four sides which connect with bolted

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.340
steel rods and glue.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:53.700
After closing up the ends with wood panels,
workers install wood support bars, which will

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:58.980
reinforce the table and after a goal, direct
the ball to the ball return tray.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:08.040
The table now goes to the paint shop where
workers either stay in the wood or leave it

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:14.250
natural. For this model, they also spray red
stain into the recessed stripes and logo.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:22.650
All tables receive a finishing code of
transparent varnish to protect the wood.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:26.530
They install the sloped ball return panel.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:32.440
When a player scores, the ball rolls down
the panel to an aluminum ball return tray.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:39.060
After sliding the plywood table bottom into
place, workers turn the table right side up.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:43.110
Mount the aluminum goal nets and the scoring
units right behind them.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:51.030
Then they lay the playing surface made of
green vinyl on pressed wood on top of the

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.470
wooden support bars.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.020
Wood trim around the perimeter holds the
surface in place.

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:05.320
A worker mounts the players for each line
onto a hollow stainless steel rod using a

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.030
template to space them correctly.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:12.160
He bolts each player to the rod, then
attaches a rubber bumper to the players at

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:16.300
each end to prevent them from slamming
against the side walls.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:23.050
He inserts a narrower stainless steel rod
into the hollow bar to make it telescopic.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:31.930
After preparing eight rounds of players, a
worker installs them in the table.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:37.840
The telescoping handle end of the rod has a
spring loaded bearing that fits in a hole in

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.990
the table. He secures it from the outside.

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:47.240
After bolting the opposite end, workers
protect the top edge of the table with a

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.350
plastic trim.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.740
After threading plastic handles to the
telescopic end of the rods and mounting the

00:04:54.740 --> 00:05:01.040
tables on four sturdy, solid wood legs, this
foosball table is ready for kickoff.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:08.910
Marseille Soap is a vegetable oil based
soap, first handcrafted in the port city of

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.190
Marseille, France, in the Middle Ages.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:17.310
This gentle, hypoallergenic all purpose
block soap became prized across Europe for

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:21.420
washing clothes, dishes, floors and
cleansing oneself.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:27.030
Marseilles soap is crafted from just four
traditional ingredients with no animal fats,

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.670
colorants perfumes or preservatives.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:34.020
It's still produced today, as it has been
for more than 600 years.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:38.730
The four ingredients are sea salt water.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:47.690
On the right caustic soda and either coconut
oil, palm oil or most often, olive pomace

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:52.610
oil. The second oil extracted from olives
after they've been pressed to extract virgin

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.170
olive oil for consumption.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:02.520
A worker releases the required quantities of
oil and caustic soda into a cooking cauldron,

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:07.260
then brings the mixture to a boil while
stirring for 1 to 2 days.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:12.960
The fatty acids in the oil react to the
alkaline caustic soda, producing a thick soap

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.420
paste containing glycerin, a natural
compound.

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.380
This transformation is known as
Saponification.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:28.130
Workers add more caustic soda and cook at
248°F for another day.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:35.780
They wash the paste with salt water 2 or 3
times each, washing lasting half a day.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:40.190
This removes impurities and glycerine
without glycerine.

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:44.540
The soap has better detergent power to
remove grease stains on fabric.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:52.260
Next. Over the course of a day, the workers
repeatedly rinse the boiling soap paste with

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:55.230
fresh water. Then they let it set for two
days.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:07:03.270
They reheat the paste for about ten minutes
at 158°F, just to soften it enough to be

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.280
pumped to a series of superheaters.

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:15.060
The superheaters heat the paste to 230°F
liquefying it.

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:21.280
As the liquid soap leaves the last
superheater, it passes through a nozzle which

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:23.590
sprays it onto the walls of an atomizer.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:29.940
The atomizer calls the soap under vacuum,
solidifying it into a dry moldable

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:37.400
consistency. Motorized blades, then scrape
the dried soap from the atomizer walls.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:44.150
The soap falls directly into an extrusion
machine, which works much like a pasta maker.

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:52.550
The machine forces the soap through small
round dies as revolving blades chop it into

00:07:52.550 --> 00:08:02.070
noodles. As the soap noodles fall onto the
conveyor belt, the soap workshop chief

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:06.180
inspects the quality by assessing the
colour, the aroma and the texture.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:15.270
At the company's in-house lab, a technician
conducts quality control tests on samples

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:17.100
drawn from each production run.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:22.200
In this test, he measures the percentage of
pure soap.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:28.130
He weighs the sample, then heats it in a
microwave oven for ten minutes to evaporate

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:29.150
all the moisture.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:36.060
This leaves only pure soap without water.

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:40.570
He relays the sample to calculate the
percentage of pure soap.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:44.270
As well as the oil content, which must be
72%.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:52.760
The factory sells a portion of its Marseille
soap noodles to companies who mold their own

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:59.630
soap bars. It also molds a house brand right
here, compressing the noodles into a

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:05.930
homogeneous paste, then extruding a long
continuous bar, an automated guillotine

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:08.270
slices the bar into the selected shape.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:16.960
The conveyor belt ferries the cubes to the
stamping machine, which stamps all six sides.

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:20.630
Each cue bears the company's name and logo.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:26.180
The soap's oil content and the Savon de
Marseille designation, attesting that this is

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:29.450
indeed authentic, traditionally made
Marseilles soap.

